# Compilation units of binutils 2.41 that bk-binutils-sys builds.
#
# One path per line, relative to the binutils source root. This file is the
# single source of truth: scripts/vendor-binutils.sh vendors these files plus
# every file they #include, and build.rs compiles exactly these files.
#
# How the list was derived (docs/features/gnu-disasm.md, "Build"):
# binutils was configured with --enable-targets=all and a program calling
# disassembler(), disassemble_init_for_target() and bfd_scan_arch() was
# linked against libopcodes.a; the linker map named the objects it pulled in.
# From libopcodes those are all of them except aarch64-asm.c, aarch64-asm-2.c,
# cris-desc.c, lm32-opinst.c, m32r-opinst.c, msp430-decode.c and visium-opc.c.
# From libbfd only the architecture tables and byte-order helpers are taken;
# the BFD entry points that need an object file are provided by
# shim/bfd_nofile.c instead of the 290 objects libbfd would otherwise add.

# --- libopcodes: common
opcodes/dis-buf.c
opcodes/dis-init.c
opcodes/disassemble.c

# --- libopcodes: per target (TARGET32_LIBOPCODES_CFILES and
# TARGET64_LIBOPCODES_CFILES of opcodes/Makefile.am)
